摘要中的主要功能必须被所选片段支持。优先把改变用途含义的条件写进摘要，不能只藏在limitations。遇到“阶段1骨架”“cloud provider待实现”“匿名thread后续实现”等，摘要明确当前仅本地草稿/审批落盘，不说已实现匿名网络或云端发布。Codex/模型登录适配归coding-development；Oopz等语音房的对话连接归communication-integrations。自述兼容或性能用“作者称/README注明”，不冒充本次验证。
格式示例（仅结构，不是来源事实）：evidence:[{"paragraph_id":"p3s1","fact":"该片段支持的中文转述"}]。请从本次真实输入挑选编号。","role":"system"},{"content":"{"metadata":{"description":"一个可以管理皮肤的dsh插件","id":"gh:1334951659","install_available":true,"language":"JavaScript","name":"dsh-skin-manager","slug":"xiaoyangcheng84-svg/dsh-skin-manager","topics":["dsh-plugin"]},"paragraphs":[{"id":"p1s1","text":"# dsh-skin-manager"},{"id":"p2s1","text":"English | 中文"},{"id":"p3s1","text":"A lightweight **skin manager** for the DeepSeek Harness web GUI. It discovers\nevery installed skin ("},{"id":"p3s2","text":"any package carrying a `skin.json` plus a prebuilt\nclient bundle), lists them in a dedicated **Setti"},{"id":"p3s3","text":"ngs → Skins** page, and lets\nyou switch the active skin with one click — mutually exclusive, hot-rel"},{"id":"p3s4","text":"oaded\nwithout restarting `dsh web`."},{"id":"p4s1","text":"## Features"},{"id":"p5s1","text":"- **Dynamic discovery** — scans the web profile's `node_modules` for packages\nwith `skin.json` + pre"},{"id":"p5s2","text":"built `lib/client.js`, and also recognizes market\nthemes without `skin.json` (a client bundle plus a"},{"id":"p5s3","text":" `cordis.patch.yml` that\ninserts a theme/skin loader row, e.g. `dsh-skin` / Codex-style skin or\n`dsh"},{"id":"p5s4","text":"-kimino-theme`). Newly installed skins appear automatically; no registry\nregeneration, no code chang"},{"id":"p5s5","text":"es.\n- **Dedicated settings page** — a `settings.section` entry (id `skins`,\norder 20) in the setting"},{"id":"p5s6","text":"s sidebar, next to General / Models.\n- **One-click apply** — pick a skin and click **Apply**; the pr"},{"id":"p5s7","text":"ofile patch is\nrewritten and DSH's config watcher hot-reloads it within seconds. Refresh\nthe page to"},{"id":"p5s8","text":" activate.\n- **Mutually exclusive** — exactly one skin is active at a time (the active\none gets an `"},{"id":"p5s9","text":"insert` row, every other skin a `disabled: true` row).\n- **Restore default** — the **Default** optio"},{"id":"p5s10","text":"n disables every skin and returns\nto the stock DeepSeek Harness appearance."},{"id":"p6s1","text":"## Install"},{"id":"p7s1","text":"[代码示例省略，未执行]"},{"id":"p8s1","text":"Then restart `dsh web` (or rely on the market's hot install). Open\n**Settings → Skins** after a page"},{"id":"p8s2","text":"art `dsh web` (or rely on the market's hot install). Open\n**Settings → Skins** after a page refresh."},{"id":"p9s1","text":"> Requires git for the `github:` source install; alternatively install from a\n> local checkout with "},{"id":"p9s2","text":"`dsh plugin --profile web add link:<path>`."},{"id":"p10s1","text":"## Usage"},{"id":"p11s1","text":"1. Open **Settings → Skins**.\n2. See **Default** plus every installed skin (e.g. 深海女仆工坊 / maid-ateli"},{"id":"p11s2","text":"er).\n3. Click **Apply** on a skin → click **Refresh** when prompted → the skin\nactivates.\n4. Click *"},{"id":"p11s3","text":"*Apply** on **Default** to restore the stock look."},{"id":"p12s1","text":"## Skin package protocol"},{"id":"p13s1","text":"Any package is recognized as a skin when:"},{"id":"p14s1","text":"- it lives under the profile's `node_modules` (top-level or `@scope/name`),\n- it ships a `skin.json`"},{"id":"p14s2","text":" (`id`, `name`, `package`, `accent`, `bodyAttr`,\n`tagline`, optional `wiring.id` — the same fields u"},{"id":"p14s3","text":"sed by\ndsh-deep-whale / dsh-web-ui skins), and\n- it ships a prebuilt client bundle (`exports[\"./clie"},{"id":"p14s4","text":"nt\"]` or `lib/client.js`)."},{"id":"p15s1","text":"A market theme without `skin.json` is also recognized when:"},{"id":"p16s1","text":"- it has `dsh.client` and `dsh.bundle.patch`,\n- its `cordis.patch.yml` contains a simple `insert` ro"},{"id":"p16s2","text":"w,\n- the package name, row id, or (for immediately-loaded client bundles)\ndescription/keywords menti"},{"id":"p16s3","text":"on theme/skin, and\n- it ships a prebuilt client bundle."},{"id":"p17s1","text":"## dsh-market coordination"},{"id":"p18s1","text":"When dsh-market is installed, applying a skin from this manager also:"},{"id":"p19s1","text":"- rewrites the same `cordis.patch.yml` managed section (boot persistence),\n- updates dsh-market's `."},{"id":"p19s2","text":"dsh-market/state.json` so it cannot re-disable the\nchosen skin at boot,\n- unmounts stale dsh-market "},{"id":"p19s3","text":"hot mounts that would otherwise overlap the newly\napplied skin, and\n- syncs dsh-market's in-memory d"},{"id":"p19s4","text":"isabled state before rewriting the patch, so\nthe market's self-healing guard cannot immediately re-d"},{"id":"p19s5","text":"isable the skin you\njust applied — no manual \"use\" click in the market is needed."},{"id":"p20s1","text":"## How switching works"},{"id":"p21s1","text":"Switching rewrites the managed section of the profile's `cordis.patch.yml`\n(between `# --- dsh-skin-"},{"id":"p21s2","text":"manager managed ---` markers):"},{"id":"p22s1","text":"- active skin → an `- insert:` row;\n- every other skin → `- id: <rowId>` + `disabled: true`."},{"id":"p23s1","text":"Non-skin user patch rows (e.g. dsh-market) are preserved untouched."},{"id":"p24s1","text":"## API"},{"id":"p25s1","text":"The host half mounts three routes under `/api/skin-manager`:"},{"id":"p26s1","text":"| Route | Method | Purpose |"},{"id":"p27s1","text":"| `/api/skin-manager/list` | GET | List installed skins + current active id |\n| `/api/skin-manager/a"},{"id":"p27s2","text":"pply` | POST | `{ id }` or `{ id: \"official\" }` to switch |\n| `/api/skin-manager/bundle` | GET | `?i"},{"id":"p27s3","text":"d=<skinId>` serve a skin's client bundle |"},{"id":"p28s1","text":"## Development"},{"id":"p29s1","text":"The client bundle is written directly in the `__ModuleLoader__` bundle format\n(the same shape tsdown"},{"id":"p29s2","text":" emits for the shipped `ui-*` packages), so no build\nstep is required. `lib/client.js` may `require`"},{"id":"p29s3","text":" only module-table entities\n(platform seed words like `react` and registered client bundles)."},{"id":"p30s1","text":"## License"},{"id":"p31s1","text":"MIT"}],"truncated":false}","role":"user"}],"model":"MiniMax-M3.1-Flash","reasoning_effort":"low","stream":false}
